<VI _name="lvtd_discon_one.vi" description="Measurement probe\3A run Discon Typedef on ONE named front panel control and save the file in place\2C reporting what Is Typedef? said before and after and what the call itself answered.\0A\0AIT TARGETS ONE CONTROL BY LABEL ON PURPOSE. An earlier version looped over every control on the panel and called Discon Typedef on each\2C including three that were not typedefs\2C and LabVIEW died within five seconds with NO entry in its own crash log - while the same VI loaded cleanly at execState 1\2C so it was the RUN and not the file. Whether an unguarded call is what killed it is not established here\3B this probe simply does not make one.\0A\0AIt does NOT descend into the cluster. The question it exists to settle is whether disconnecting the OUTER typedef also clears one embedded inside it\2C so the descent has to be absent and the answer comes from extracting the saved file afterwards and counting what is left.\0A\0AThe three nodes are CHAINED through their error terminals\3A with the error inputs unwired they carry no data dependency and LabVIEW may run them in any order\2C which would make before and after meaningless.">
